   "finish_reason": "stop",
   "content": "The single most important finding is **F43**, which reveals that MoE concurrency is stream-diversity-bound, meaning 16 users asking different questions run 40% slower than 16 asking the same question, thereby exposing that the previously published fleet throughput of 193.5 t/s was a best-case artifact that overstated real capacity by 1.78x. This is critical because it corrects the operational understanding of the hardware's limits, showing that the box's actual serving peak is only about four concurrent users rather than the sixteen implied by earlier benchmarks. The evidence supporting this is a controlled experiment where length-matched distinct prompts caused the MoE workhorse to drop from 191.70 t/s to 108.86 t/s, while a dense model control showed no such penalty (-0.1%), proving the slowdown is caused by expert routing contention on a bandwidth-limited system.",
